		(uuid "0856e08b-c93b-4151-91b5-649c5b04228c")
		(at 30 60 -90)
		(descr "Wurth WR-COM USB 3.1 Type-C receptacle, horizontal, mid-mount (sunk 1.5 mm into a board cut-out), 24 pins: SMT row A, two through-hole rows B, four shell stakes. Land pattern from the Wurth data sheet 632723130112 rev 002.000 (2025-09-04), page 1, for a 1.6 mm board. Origin is the middle of the PCB edge, +Y towards the mating face. The data sheet draws but does not dimension the PCB edge: it is placed 0.25 mm beyond the front stake pads (5.25 mm from the lower through-hole row), which puts the mating face 2.51 mm beyond the edge (7.76 mm data sheet length to that row). The board cut-out is NOT part of the footprint; it is drawn on Dwgs.User: 9.5 mm wide, 4.70 mm deep, inner corners relieved. Shell stake pad and slot widths at the rear are taken to be the same as the dimensioned front ones. 3D model: Wurth's STEP (Download_STEP_632723130112 rev1, 2018-04-25), turned so its +Z is the mating direction and its +Y points into the board, its mating face at Y = 2.51 and its seating plane (1.6 mm above the stake tips) on the board; the opening's centre is then 0.29 mm above the board's top face.")
		(tags "USB-C Type-C receptacle mid-mount sunk Wurth WR-COM 632723130112")
